 - 2026-06-25: PHASE A2 (ARC NORTH STAR; PRIMARY; the capstone + SOTA hand-off -- ACT to disambiguate) -- HYPOTHESIS-DRIVEN ACTIVE-PROBE DISAMBIGUATION. The .434 A2 (exp4713) proved the present winner (coverage 1.0) is NOT separable from same-depth distractors by ANY static oracle-distinct feature (precision_at_k_delta=0.0) -- static selection is EXHAUSTED. The principled answer: the agent ACTS to disambiguate. E3AgentPolicy keeps a posterior over candidate goal/dynamics hypotheses, asks arc_executable_world_model what transition each predicts, and takes information-gain actions that SPLIT the posterior -- so the present-but-unseparable winner becomes distinguishable by its observed CONSEQUENCE, not a static feature. The energy verifier scores which probe best splits the posterior (oracle-distinct). Gate: the GENERIC agent reaches a NEW level via active probing on >=1 clean L1 game, offline-reproduced, with the NO-PROBE (passive) ablation FAILING. arXiv:2506.01876 + 2309.08477. live_path-reachable. live_agent_self_discovery. verifier_is_oracle:false. retire_if_same_verdict. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete: active_probe_no_new_level_residual_budget_insufficient; results/experiment_4727_active_probe_disambiguation.json
